 {%- comment -%}
  Wig Party — ONE column of a mega-menu panel.

  Extracted so the six dedicated panel types (shop / best_sellers / start_here / live /
  community / daily_deals) share a single copy of every column renderer instead of each
  repeating it. A panel is now just a short list of `render 'aria-mega-column'` calls whose
  arguments ARE the preset design values from the Figma frames.

  Column types, mapped 1:1 onto the distinct shapes in the design:
    menu_divided  26px text rows with 1px rules between      (Shop cols 2-3)
    menu_padded   outlined 58px cards, 1px #EADDD4 at r12    (Start Here / Live / Community / Deals)
    style_cards   48px thumb + title + subtitle              (Shop col 1)
    promo_card    244x315 image card, badge + full-width CTA (Shop cols 4-5)
    products      250px product cards, auto-populated        (Best Sellers / Start Here / Deals)
    feature_card  glass card on a photo OR gradient shell    (Best Sellers / Community / Deals)
    media_card    large image + signature + play affordance  (Live)
    photo_row     cream-matted photos + outlined CTA         (Community)
    items_photos  48px round thumb + one-line label, menu-fed (Shop: By Cap Construction)
    items_divided 26px text rows with 1px rules, menu-fed    (Shop: Collection / Color / Size & Length)
    lmu_schedule  menu_padded rows of the upcoming shows from LiveMeUp (Live); col_count rows,
                  each opening the reminder (or the player once on air); col_btn_url is the
                  Live page the rows link to

  Params (all optional except col_type):
    col_type, col_heading, col_icon, col_menu_handle, col_width, col_push,
    col_image, col_body, col_chip, col_chip_style, col_btn_label, col_btn_url,
    col_collection, col_count, panel_id, shopify_attributes,
    col_variant                              -- feature-card design variant:
                                                'best-sellers' | 'community' | 'deals'
    col_shell                                -- bool: wrap the column in the shared
                                                white->cream gradient shell (radius 8,
                                                20px side + bottom padding). Start Here /
                                                Deals product rows and Community's CTA
                                                column only — Best Sellers has none.
    col_icon_tone                            -- 'qi' for the #BC696B gold-sell glyph
    col_title_tone                           -- 'accent' for a Primary/Dark Pink label
    col_lmu                                  -- bool, media_card / heading: fed from LiveMeUp
                                                (assets/aria-livemeup.js) — the live, next or
                                                latest show's label, time and cover; the typed
                                                heading and image stay until the feed answers,
                                                and stay for good if it has no shows
    col_placeholders, col_placeholder_subs   -- '|'-joined Figma row labels, used only
                                                while the column's menu is missing
    placeholders                             -- the section's placeholder switch

  `col_heading` is usually only a FALLBACK: when the column is fed by a Shopify menu, that
  menu's own title wins, because every handle is named after the heading it feeds
  (header-shop-shop-by-collection -> "Shop by Collection"). The one exception is
  `items_photos`/`items_divided`: there `col_heading` is itself a merchant-set block setting,
  so it always wins over the linked menu's own admin title (see the comment above
  `col_heading` below).
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  comment
    `col_menu_handle` arrives in two shapes: a preset STRING handle for the columns whose
    menu this spec fixes, or a link_list OBJECT from a menu picker (Shop by Style, the one
    column with no supplied handle). Looking a string up in `linklists` works; passing the
    object through it yields nil, so fall back to using the object directly.
  endcomment
  assign col_menu = nil
  if col_menu_handle != blank
    assign col_menu = linklists[col_menu_handle]
    if col_menu.links.size == 0 and col_menu_handle.links.size > 0
      assign col_menu = col_menu_handle
    endif
  endif

  comment
    A link counts only when it goes somewhere: menu items saved as `#` or blank (rows whose
    page does not exist yet) are skipped, here and in every loop below. A link column with
    nothing real left is not rendered at all (see `skip_col`), so the menu never shows a
    dead row or an empty heading, and the row appears by itself once the page is linked.
  endcomment
  assign menu_has_links = false
  for link in col_menu.links
    if link.url != blank and link.url != '#'
      assign menu_has_links = true
      break
    endif
  endfor
  assign skip_col = false
  if menu_has_links == false
    if col_type == 'menu_divided' or col_type == 'menu_padded' or col_type == 'style_cards' or col_type == 'items_photos' or col_type == 'items_divided'
      assign skip_col = true
    endif
  endif
  comment
    An explicit col_heading (a merchant-set block setting, for items_photos/items_divided)
    always wins. Only fall back to the linked menu's own admin title when no heading was
    supplied at all, which is the case for every OTHER menu-fed column here (their preset
    literal heading already matches the handle's title by naming convention).
  endcomment
  if col_heading == blank and col_menu.title != blank
    assign col_heading = col_menu.title
  endif

  assign col_count_setting = col_count
  if col_chip_style == blank
    assign col_chip_style = 'white'
  endif

  comment
    FALLBACKS, so no column ever renders as a headed but empty box while the real content
    is still being produced. Three layers, most-preferred first:

    1. (Placeholder rows were removed on 2026-10-15 at the client's request: they linked to
       the catalogue, not a real page. A link column without real links is now hidden.)
    2. images - the block's own image, else a real product shot from the column's collection
       (or the catalogue), and only then Shopify's line-art placeholder. A real photo reads
       far closer to the design than a wireframe.
    3. links - a genuine destination instead of '#': the column's collection where it has
       one, otherwise the all-products route.
  endcomment
  assign fallback_url = routes.all_products_collection_url
  if col_collection != blank and col_collection.url != blank
    assign fallback_url = col_collection.url
  endif
  assign resolved_url = col_btn_url
  if resolved_url == blank
    assign resolved_url = fallback_url
  endif

  assign fallback_img = nil
  if col_image == blank
    if col_collection.products.first.featured_image != blank
      assign fallback_img = col_collection.products.first.featured_image
    elsif collections.all.products.first.featured_image != blank
      assign fallback_img = collections.all.products.first.featured_image
    endif
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Only the WIDTH travels as a custom property. There used to be a `col_height` /
  `--aria-mega-feature-h` pair here as well, from when feature-card heights were settings;
  every card height is now a design constant in the variant CSS (449 / 410 / 450), no panel
  passed it and no rule consumed it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture col_style -%}
  {%- if col_width > 0 -%}--aria-mega-col-w: {{ col_width }}px;{%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  NO PRODUCT CARDS ON MOBILE, and not rendered rather than hidden.

  The drawer's level-2 panels reuse these exact renderers, but a `products` column has no
  place in a 360px drawer — and the requirement is that the desktop product grid is not
  loaded there at all, so `display: none` would not do: the markup, the `<product-form>`
  elements and every `image_url` would still be emitted. The whole column is skipped
  instead, HEAD INCLUDED — returning just the "Best Sellers · the styles that actually
  sell" heading over an empty body would be worse than omitting it.

  This is the ONE content difference between the two presentations. Everything else adapts
  in CSS, which is why only the `products` call sites pass `col_context`. The desktop
  panels never pass it, so their product data and rendering are completely untouched.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if col_context == 'mobile' and col_type == 'products'
    assign skip_col = true
  endif
-%}
{%- unless skip_col -%}

{%- comment -%}
  `col_shell` is the white->cream gradient SHELL the design wraps around two column types:
  the Start Here / Dailey Deals product rows and the Community CTA column. It is a shared
  modifier rather than three copies of the same gradient, and it is deliberately NOT on
  every products column — Best Sellers (6337:3210) draws its row on bare white.

  `col_icon_tone` picks the glyph colour. Every column glyph is Primary/Dark Pink except
  `gold-sell`, which the design draws in Quaternary `#BC696B`.

  `col_title_tone` does the same for the label: black everywhere except the Live media
  column, whose "LIVE TONIGHT · 7:00 PM CT" is Primary/Dark Pink (node 6337:3942).
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="aria-mega__col aria-mega__col--{{ col_type | replace: '_', '-' }}{% if col_variant != blank %} aria-mega__col--feature-{{ col_variant }}{% endif %}{% if col_shell %} aria-mega__col--shell{% endif %}{% if col_push %} aria-mega__col--push{% endif %}"
  {% if col_style != blank %}style="{{ col_style }}"{% endif %}
  {{ shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- if col_heading != blank -%}
    <div class="aria-mega__col-head">
      {%- comment -%}
        ADDED 2026-10-26 — `col_icon_image` lets a column use a merchant-uploaded image
        instead of the built-in `aria-icon` sprite (used by the 3 new Shop filter columns,
        each of which has its own image_picker setting). Existing calls never pass this, so
        every column keeps using the sprite via the unchanged `elsif` below.

        `col_icon_fallback` is a theme asset filename shown while that image_picker is still
        empty (its Figma-downloaded default) — a plain `asset_url`, not `image_url`, because
        Shopify's image_picker can only default to an already-uploaded Shopify Files image,
        never to a theme asset file.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if col_icon_image != blank -%}
        {{
          col_icon_image
          | image_url: width: 48
          | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '24,48', width: 24, height: 24, class: 'aria-mega__col-icon', alt: ''
        }}
      {%- elsif col_icon_fallback != blank -%}
        <img
          src="{{ col_icon_fallback | asset_url }}"
          width="24"
          height="24"
          alt=""
          loading="lazy"
          class="aria-mega__col-icon"
        >
      {%- elsif col_icon != blank and col_icon != 'none' -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign icon_class = 'aria-mega__col-icon'
          if col_icon_tone != blank
            assign icon_class = icon_class | append: ' aria-mega__col-icon--' | append: col_icon_tone
          endif
        -%}
        {%- render 'aria-icon', name: col_icon, class: icon_class -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      <span
        class="aria-mega__col-title{% if col_title_tone != blank %} aria-mega__col-title--{{ col_title_tone }}{% endif %}"
        {% if col_type == 'items_photos' or col_type == 'items_divided' %}title="{{ col_heading }}"{% endif %}
      >
        {%- if col_lmu -%}
          <span data-lmu-fallback>{{ col_heading }}</span>
          <span data-lmu-featured="live-first" hidden>
            <span data-lmu-if="live">{{ 'aria_theme.live.lmu.menu_live' | t }}</span>
            <span data-lmu-if="upcoming">{{ 'aria_theme.live.lmu.menu_next' | t }} · <span data-lmu-date="short"></span></span>
            <span data-lmu-if="replay">{{ 'aria_theme.live.lmu.menu_replay' | t }} · <span data-lmu-date="day"></span></span>
          </span>
        {%- else -%}
          {{- col_heading -}}
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- case col_type -%}
    {%- when 'menu_divided' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        V4 Shop cols 2-3: 26px rows, 12px apart, a 1px #d9d9d9 rule BETWEEN rows and
        not after the last. The rule is drawn with a border on every row except the
        last rather than as separate elements, so an odd item count cannot leave a
        dangling line.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if menu_has_links -%}
        <ul class="aria-mega__links aria-mega__links--divided" role="list">
          {%- for link in col_menu.links -%}
            {%- if link.url == blank or link.url == '#' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
            <li class="aria-mega__links-item">
              <a
                href="{% render 'aria-link-url', url: link.url %}"
                class="aria-mega__link"
                {% if link.current %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
              >{{ link.title }}</a>
              {%- if link.links.size > 0 -%}
                {%- render 'aria-mega-sublinks', link: link -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- when 'menu_padded' -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        V4 Start Here / Live / Community / Deals: 58px rows on a 70px pitch (so a
        12px gap), label inset 12px from the left. The row is the hit area, which is
        why the padding lives on the <a> and not on the <li>.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if menu_has_links -%}
        <ul class="aria-mega__links aria-mega__links--padded" role="list">
          {%- for link in col_menu.links -%}
            {%- if link.url == blank or link.url == '#' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
            <li class="aria-mega__links-item">
              <a
                href="{% render 'aria-link-url', url: link.url %}"
                class="aria-mega__link"
                {% if link.current %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
              >{{ link.title }}</a>
              {%- if link.links.size > 0 -%}
                {%- render 'aria-mega-sublinks', link: link -%}
              {%- endif -%}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- when 'lmu_schedule' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Live "This Week's Schedule": the upcoming shows scheduled in the LiveMeUp app, drawn
        as the same outlined rows as menu_padded ("Tue 7:00 PM · New Arrivals"). A row sets a
        reminder (or plays the show once it is on air); with no show booked, one row points
        at the Live page instead. Filled by assets/aria-livemeup.js when the menu first opens.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div data-lmu-list data-lmu-source="upcoming" data-lmu-limit="{{ col_count | default: 4 }}">
        <template data-lmu-template>
          <li class="aria-mega__links-item">
            <a href="{{ col_btn_url }}" class="aria-mega__link aria-mega__link--lmu" data-lmu-href="{{ col_btn_url }}" data-lmu-action>
              <span class="aria-mega__lmu-when" data-lmu-if="upcoming" data-lmu-date="short"></span>
              <span class="aria-mega__lmu-when" data-lmu-if="live">{{ 'aria_theme.live.lmu.menu_live' | t }}</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
              <span class="aria-mega__lmu-title" data-lmu-title></span>
            </a>
          </li>
        </template>
        <ul class="aria-mega__links aria-mega__links--padded" role="list" data-lmu-items>
          {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
            <li class="aria-mega__links-item" data-lmu-loading aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="aria-mega__link aria-lmu-skeleton">&nbsp;</span>
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
        <ul class="aria-mega__links aria-mega__links--padded" role="list" data-lmu-list-empty hidden>
          <li class="aria-mega__links-item">
            <a href="{{ col_btn_url }}" class="aria-mega__link">{{ 'aria_theme.live.lmu.menu_none' | t }}</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    {%- when 'style_cards' -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        V4 Shop col 1: 48x48 thumbnail + title + subtitle. A Shopify menu only
        carries a title and a URL, so the thumbnail and subtitle are pulled from the
        linked RESOURCE instead of being hardcoded: `link.object` is the collection
        (or product) the menu item points at, giving us its image and description for
        free and keeping the column fully dynamic. Rows whose target has no image
        fall back to the tinted empty thumb, which is what V4 shows behind the photo.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if menu_has_links -%}
        <ul class="aria-mega__styles" role="list">
          {%- for link in col_menu.links -%}
            {%- if link.url == blank or link.url == '#' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign target = link.object
              assign thumb = nil
              assign subtitle = ''

              if link.type == 'collection_link' and target != nil
                if target.image != blank
                  assign thumb = target.image
                elsif target.products.first.featured_image != blank
                  assign thumb = target.products.first.featured_image
                endif
                assign subtitle = target.description | strip_html | truncate: 40
              elsif link.type == 'product_link' and target != nil
                assign thumb = target.featured_image
                assign subtitle = target.description | strip_html | truncate: 40
              endif
            -%}
            <li class="aria-mega__styles-item">
              <a href="{% render 'aria-link-url', url: link.url %}" class="aria-mega__style">
                <span class="aria-mega__style-thumb">
                  {%- if thumb != blank -%}
                    {{
                      thumb
                      | image_url: width: 96
                      | image_tag:
                        loading: 'lazy',
                        widths: '48,96',
                        class: 'aria-mega__style-img',
                        alt: ''
                    }}
                  {%- else -%}
                    <span class="aria-mega__style-img-fallback"><span></span></span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </span>
                <span class="aria-mega__style-text">
                  <span class="aria-mega__style-title">{{ link.title }}</span>
                  {%- if subtitle != blank -%}
                    <span class="aria-mega__style-sub">{{ subtitle }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </span>
              </a>
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- when 'promo_card' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        V4 Shop cols 4-5: a 244x315 image card with a chip pinned top-left and a
        full-width 36px terracotta CTA welded to the bottom edge.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <a href="{{ resolved_url }}" class="aria-mega__promo">
        <span class="aria-mega__promo-media">
          {%- if col_image != blank -%}
            {{
              col_image
              | image_url: width: 640
              | image_tag:
                loading: 'lazy',
                widths: '244,488,640',
                sizes: '(max-width: 1279px) 92vw, 244px',
                class: 'aria-mega__promo-img',
                alt: col_image.alt | default: col_heading
            }}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- if fallback_img != blank -%}
              {{ fallback_img | image_url: width: 640 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '244,488,640', sizes: '(max-width: 1279px) 92vw, 244px', class: 'aria-mega__promo-img', alt: '' }}
            {%- else -%}
              {{ 'collection-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'aria-mega__promo-img aria-mega__promo-img--placeholder' }}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
        {%- if col_chip != blank -%}
          <span class="aria-mega__chip aria-mega__chip--{{ col_chip_style | default: 'white' }}">{{ col_chip }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if col_btn_label != blank -%}
          <span class="aria-mega__promo-cta">{{ col_btn_label }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </a>

    {%- when 'products' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        V4 Best Sellers / Start Here / Deals: a row of 250px product cards.

        AUTOMATIC by design — there is no manual product list. The source is resolved
        in this order, and in every case the products come out in the COLLECTION's own
        sort order, so setting that collection to "Best selling" in Admin is what makes
        this a live best-seller feed that re-orders itself as sales change:
          1. the block's collection setting, when the merchant picked one
          2. a collection handled `best-sellers`, if the store has one
          3. `collections.all` as the last resort so the column is never empty
        Sold-out and unavailable products are skipped; draft products are never
        exposed to Liquid in the first place.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign source = nil
        if col_collection != blank and col_collection.products.size > 0
          assign source = col_collection
        elsif collections['best-sellers'].products.size > 0
          assign source = collections['best-sellers']
        else
          assign source = collections.all
        endif

        assign wanted = col_count_setting | default: 4
        assign shown = 0
      -%}
      {%- if source.products.size > 0 -%}
        <div class="aria-mega__products">
          {%- for product in source.products -%}
            {%- if shown >= wanted -%}
              {%- break -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- unless product.available -%}
              {%- continue -%}
            {%- endunless -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign shown = shown | plus: 1
              assign card_sub = product.type | default: product.vendor
              capture card_sub
                render 'aria-strip-supplier', text: card_sub
              endcapture
              capture card_title
                render 'aria-strip-supplier', text: product.title
              endcapture
              capture card_image_alt
                render 'aria-strip-supplier', text: product.featured_image.alt
              endcapture
            -%}
            <div class="aria-mega__product">
              <a href="{{ product.url }}" class="aria-mega__product-media">
                {%- if product.featured_image != blank -%}
                  {{
                    product.featured_image
                    | image_url: width: 640
                    | image_tag:
                      loading: 'lazy',
                      widths: '250,500,640',
                      class: 'aria-mega__product-img',
                      alt: card_image_alt
                  }}
                {%- else -%}
                  {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'aria-mega__product-img' }}
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  The badge is a RANK -- node 6337:3222 reads literally "#1" in amber
                  on the first card. So the default is the position in the row, which
                  makes it self-maintaining as the best-seller order changes. The
                  column's chip setting overrides it where the design shows copy
                  instead (Deals uses "Dailey Deal").
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  The design badges these cards from PRODUCT data, not one fixed string: card 1 reads
                  "-30%", card 2 "DEAL", card 3 its collection name. So a product actually on
                  sale shows its own discount in amber (exactly card 1), otherwise the
                  column's badge setting applies, and failing that the best-seller rank.
                  One fixed label on every card was wrong.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign badge_style = col_chip_style
                  if product.compare_at_price > product.price
                    assign pct = product.compare_at_price | minus: product.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: product.compare_at_price | round
                    assign badge_text = '−' | append: pct | append: '%'
                    assign badge_style = 'amber'
                  elsif col_chip != blank
                    assign badge_text = col_chip
                  else
                    assign badge_text = '#' | append: shown
                    assign badge_style = 'amber'
                  endif
                -%}
                <span class="aria-mega__chip aria-mega__chip--{{ badge_style | default: 'white' }}">{{ badge_text }}</span>
                <span class="aria-mega__product-title">{{ card_title }}</span>
              </a>
              {%- comment -%}
                The cart tile carries a photo (node 6337:3225). The image is handed to
                it as a custom property on this row rather than as markup, because the
                button itself comes from the shared `aria-product-card-quick-add`
                snippet and custom properties inherit into it.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <div
                class="aria-mega__product-foot"
                {% if product.featured_image != blank %}style="--aria-mega-cart-img: url({{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 120 }});"{% endif %}
              >
                {%- render 'aria-product-card-quick-add',
                  product: product,
                  section_id: panel_id,
                  is_sold_out: false,
                  icon: 'mega-cart-02',
                  product_name: card_title
                -%}
                <div class="aria-mega__product-meta">
                  {%- if card_sub != blank -%}
                    <span class="aria-mega__product-sub">{{ card_sub }}</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  <span class="aria-mega__product-price">{{ product.price | money }}</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- when 'feature_card' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The design nests a glass card inside a shell. The shell is this column itself;
        when a PHOTO is set it becomes the shell's backdrop.

        COMMUNITY HAS NO PHOTO (node 6337:4243) — its shell is the white->cream gradient
        and nothing else. Rendering the block's image here regardless is what made the
        Community card look like a copy of Best Sellers: an absolutely positioned photo
        covered the gradient and the glass panel then read as a dark photo card. The
        image setting stays in the schema (harmless, and the variant may want it later);
        this variant simply does not draw it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- unless col_variant == 'community' -%}
        {%- if col_image == blank and fallback_img != blank -%}
          {{ fallback_img | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '300,600,900', sizes: '(max-width: 1279px) 92vw, 380px', class: 'aria-mega__feature-shell-img', alt: '' }}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if col_image != blank -%}
          {{
            col_image
            | image_url: width: 900
            | image_tag:
              loading: 'lazy',
              widths: '300,600,900',
              sizes: '(max-width: 1279px) 92vw, 380px',
              class: 'aria-mega__feature-shell-img',
              alt: col_image.alt | default: ''
          }}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endunless -%}
      <div class="aria-mega__feature">
        <div class="aria-mega__feature-body">
          {%- if col_chip != blank -%}
            <p class="aria-mega__feature-title">{{ col_chip }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if col_body != blank -%}
            <p class="aria-mega__feature-text">{{ col_body }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        {%- if col_variant == 'community' -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Node 6337:4249 — the heart + "Kristi" script sits between the body copy and the
            CTA, CENTRED in the card at its own 249x96.247. Same artwork the Live media
            card uses at 120x46.384, so both go through `aria-mega-signature`.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- render 'aria-mega-signature', width: 249, height: 96.247 -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if col_btn_label != blank -%}
          <a href="{{ resolved_url }}" class="aria-mega__btn">{{ col_btn_label }}</a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

    {%- when 'media_card' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Live right column (node 6337:3937): a 493 x 414.63 image at radius 8 carrying TWO
        overlays — the white Kristi signature 16px in from the bottom-left (6337:3949) and
        a 48px play affordance 16px in from the bottom-right (6337:3950). Both were
        missing/wrong: there was no signature at all, and the play glyph was a solid
        terracotta disc rather than the design's frosted one.

        Rendered as a link rather than a video element so the panel stays lightweight —
        the destination is the live stream.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <a
        href="{{ resolved_url }}"
        class="aria-mega__media"
        {% if col_lmu %}
          data-lmu-featured="live-first"
          data-lmu-keep
          data-lmu-action
          data-lmu-upcoming-link
          data-lmu-href="{{ resolved_url }}"
        {% endif %}
      >
        {%- if col_image != blank -%}
          {{
            col_image
            | image_url: width: 1000
            | image_tag:
              loading: 'lazy',
              widths: '493,986,1000',
              sizes: '(max-width: 1279px) 92vw, 493px',
              class: 'aria-mega__media-img',
              alt: col_image.alt | default: col_heading
          }}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- if fallback_img != blank -%}
            {{ fallback_img | image_url: width: 1000 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '493,986,1000', sizes: '(max-width: 1279px) 92vw, 493px', class: 'aria-mega__media-img', alt: '' }}
          {%- else -%}
            {{ 'lifestyle-2' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'aria-mega__media-img' }}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if col_lmu -%}
          {%- comment -%} The show's own cover from LiveMeUp, laid over the typed photo once it loads. {%- endcomment -%}
          <span data-lmu-cover="493"></span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- render 'aria-mega-signature', width: 120, height: 46.384, class: 'aria-mega__signature--media' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          `wp-play-button.svg` IS node 6337:3950 (its own frame name, "Frame 2147239667",
          is still in the file) — a 70px frosted disc, `#C0C0C0` at 50% behind a 16.7px
          backdrop blur, with a rounded white triangle. The theme already ships it and
          two other sections already use it, so it is reused here at the design's 48px
          rather than redrawn as an inline glyph.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="aria-mega__media-play">
          <img
            src="{{ 'wp-play-button.svg' | asset_url }}"
            alt=""
            width="48"
            height="48"
            loading="lazy"
          >
        </span>
        {%- if col_btn_label != blank -%}
          <span class="visually-hidden">{{ col_btn_label }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </a>

    {%- when 'photo_row' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Community middle column (node 6337:4259): three photos whose middle frame is
        taller than its neighbours, then a CTA. The photos come from the linked
        collection's products so the row stays dynamic; the middle one is scaled up
        by CSS rather than by three separate image settings.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign photo_source = col_collection
      -%}
      <div class="aria-mega__photos">
        {%- if photo_source.products.size > 0 -%}
          {%- for product in photo_source.products limit: 3 -%}
            <span class="aria-mega__photo">
              {%- if product.featured_image != blank -%}
                {%- capture photo_alt -%}{%- render 'aria-strip-supplier', text: product.featured_image.alt -%}{%- endcapture -%}
                {{
                  product.featured_image
                  | image_url: width: 400
                  | image_tag:
                    loading: 'lazy',
                    widths: '176,352,400',
                    sizes: '(max-width: 1279px) 30vw, 176px',
                    class: 'aria-mega__photo-img',
                    alt: photo_alt
                }}
              {%- else -%}
                {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'aria-mega__photo-img' }}
              {%- endif -%}
            </span>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- for product in collections.all.products limit: 3 -%}
            <span class="aria-mega__photo">
              {%- if product.featured_image != blank -%}
                {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 400 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '176,352,400', sizes: '(max-width: 1279px) 30vw, 176px', class: 'aria-mega__photo-img', alt: '' }}
              {%- else -%}
                {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'aria-mega__photo-img' }}
              {%- endif -%}
            </span>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
      {%- if col_btn_label != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Node 6337:4269 — 211x54, outlined, sentence case, and it carries a trailing
          arrow ("See the gallery  →"). The arrow is NOT added here: the block's own
          button-label setting already ends in "→", so rendering an icon as well printed
          two of them. Left to the label, which is where the copy belongs.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <a href="{{ resolved_url }}" class="aria-mega__btn aria-mega__btn--outline">{{ col_btn_label }}</a>
      {%- endif -%}

    {%- when 'items_photos' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        UPDATED 2026-10-26 — Shop > By Cap Construction (Figma 7169:2960/2966) now reads its
        items from the column's own Shopify menu (`col_menu`, set via the `cap_menu` link_list
        setting): top-level links only (a menu's nested children are not shown here), first
        10, label = link.title, url = link.url. Reuses `.aria-mega__styles`' list spacing
        (48px row pitch 60, no divider) and `.aria-mega__link`'s hover/focus colour.

        The thumbnail is POSITIONAL, not from the menu (a menu item carries no image): the
        Nth visible link shows `col_item_prefix` + N + `_image` (slots 1-6). `col_default_images`
        is a '|'-joined fallback shown via `asset_url` for a slot whose picker is still empty
        (slots 1-4 default to the 4 downloaded Figma thumbnails; slot 5, 6, and any slot the
        client clears, show the plain tinted circle instead, since Shopify's image_picker can
        only default to an already-uploaded Shopify Files image, never a theme asset file).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign item_default_images = col_default_images | split: '|'
        assign item_shown = 0
      -%}
      <ul class="aria-mega__styles" role="list">
        {%- for link in col_menu.links -%}
          {%- if link.url == blank or link.url == '#' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- if item_shown >= 10 -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign item_shown = item_shown | plus: 1
            assign item_index = item_shown | minus: 1
            assign item_key_image = col_item_prefix | append: item_shown | append: '_image'
            assign item_image = block.settings[item_key_image]
            assign item_image_fallback = item_default_images[item_index]
          -%}
          <li class="aria-mega__links-item">
            <a href="{% render 'aria-link-url', url: link.url %}" class="aria-mega__link aria-mega__link--photo" title="{{ link.title }}">
              <span class="aria-mega__link-thumb">
                {%- if item_image != blank -%}
                  {{
                    item_image
                    | image_url: width: 96
                    | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '48,96', class: 'aria-mega__link-thumb-img', alt: ''
                  }}
                {%- elsif item_image_fallback != blank -%}
                  <img
                    src="{{ item_image_fallback | asset_url }}"
                    width="48"
                    height="48"
                    alt=""
                    loading="lazy"
                    class="aria-mega__link-thumb-img"
                  >
                {%- else -%}
                  <span class="aria-mega__link-thumb-empty"></span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
              <span class="aria-mega__link-label">{{ link.title }}</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>

    {%- when 'items_divided' -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        UPDATED 2026-10-26 — Shop > Shop by Collection / Shop by Color / By Size & Length
        (Figma 7169:2996, 7169:3033, 7169:3062) now read their items straight off the
        column's own Shopify menu (`col_menu`, set via each block's `*_menu` link_list
        setting): top-level links only (a menu's nested children are not shown here), first
        10, label = link.title, url = link.url. Reuses the existing 26px-row / 12px-gap /
        1px-rule styling already built for Shop by Collection (`.aria-mega__links--divided`).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <ul class="aria-mega__links aria-mega__links--divided" role="list">
        {%- assign item_shown = 0 -%}
        {%- for link in col_menu.links -%}
          {%- if link.url == blank or link.url == '#' -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- if item_shown >= 10 -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- assign item_shown = item_shown | plus: 1 -%}
          <li class="aria-mega__links-item">
            <a
              href="{% render 'aria-link-url', url: link.url %}"
              class="aria-mega__link"
              title="{{ link.title }}"
              {% if link.current %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
            ><span class="aria-mega__link-label">{{ link.title }}</span></a>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
  {%- endcase -%}
</div>

{%- endunless -%}
